;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[ExtraStages]
 ;Put extra stages here. They will be available in modes that allow selecting
 ;stage manually. For example, you can insert "stages/mybg.def.
 ;
 ;Zipped stages are also supported.
 ;Place the ZIP file in the stages/ directory. The syntax is as
 ;follows:
 ; zipname.zip/defname.def
 ;For example, if you have suavestage.def in suave.zip, the syntax is:
 ; suave.zip/suavestage.def
 ;If your def file has the same name as the zip file (eg. suave.def
 ;in suave.zip), you can just put the name of the zip file alone:
 ; suave.zip
 ;
 ;Optional parameters may follow on the same line, separated by commas.
 ;Each parameter has the form:
 ; paramname = paramvalue
 ;where paramname is the name of the parameter type, and paramvalue is the value
 ;to assign that parameter. The optional parameters are:
 ;
 ; - music
 ; Set the paramvalue to the music file path that should be used at the start
 ; of the first round. Paramvalue can be followed by optional space-separated
 ; int values: volume, loopstart and loopend.
 ; This appends the stage DEF bgmusic (and related bgmusic.*) assignment.
 ; Multiple parameters of the same type may be defined; one will be chosen
 ; at random. Unless stated otherwise, these rules also apply to other *.music
 ; parameters.

 ; - round<roundno>.music
 ; IKEMEN feature: Music used at the start of the chosen round.

 ; - final.music
 ; IKEMEN feature: Music used at the start of the final round.

 ; - life.music
 ; IKEMEN feature: Music used when the player-controlled character has
 ; (by default) less than 30% life during the deciding round (only affects
 ; the side that is at risk of being defeated). Further adjustments are
 ; available via the stage DEF file.

 ; - victory.music
 ; IKEMEN feature: Music that starts right after winner character scores the
 ; final round K.O. and continues throughout the victory screen. Unlike other
 ; music parameters, victory.music also works in Versus-type modes.
 ;
 ; - order
 ; IKEMEN feature: Set the paramvalue to the ordering priority to give the
 ; stage in Arcade and Time Attack modes. If there is at least 1 stage with
 ; assigned order, facing opponent with the exact order paramvalue will result
 ; in stage being randomly chosen from stages with the matching order. Stages
 ; can have multiple order parameters assigned at the same time.
 ;
 ; - unlock
 ; IKEMEN feature: paramvalue is executed as Lua code condition, right after
 ; new game mode is initiated and upon returning to main menu. If it evaluates
 ; to boolean 'true' the stage will become manually selectable. On 'false' it
 ; will be hidden. Due to parameters syntax, 'unlock' has to be the very last
 ; parameter used in line (everything that follows is treated as a pure Lua
 ; code). Default: true.
 ; https://github.com/ikemen-engine/Ikemen-GO/wiki/Miscellaneous-Info#lua_unlock
 ;
 ;Examples:
 ; stages/mybg.def, music=sound/song.mp3, music=sound/song2.mp3
 ; stages/mybg.def, order=3
 ;
 ;Insert your stages below.

